    <div class="measure">
      <h2>The lesson</h2>
      <p>Don't take your simple designs for granted. I almost didn't file this one, and I'm glad Chad pushed. Each piece on its own looked ordinary: a probe feed, a stacked patch, a slot. What was new was getting one probe, circular polarization, two bands and a small footprint in the same element, with edges clean enough to pack elements close together. If you have a design like that sitting on a shelf, look at the prior art before you decide it isn't novel.</p>
      <p>Patent (Google Patents): <a href="https://patents.google.com/patent/US12562485B2/en">US 12,562,485 B2</a></p>
